cements and are not scaled or decomposed.","For indexed TLSU, RegSrc0 is the unsigned per-PE GM base. When the first B.IOR is not a legacy GPR ExecutionMask record, the selector pair (RegSrc1, RegSrc2)=(0,0) means no range descriptor; any other pair selects full-width S64 MinIndexGPR and MaxIndexGPR relative byte displacements. The one-record ExecMaskPresent form keeps its legacy Base-plus-mask meaning. A descriptor with a GPR ExecutionMask uses an unflagged Base/Min/Max first record and one final contiguous mask record with ExecMaskPresent=1."],"encoding_class":"standalone-encoded","examples":["BSTART.MGATHER DataType; B.DATR PadValue, Layout (optional); B.DIM LB0=ValidCol; B.DIM LB1=ValidRow (optional); B.DIM LB2=Col (optional); B.IOT IndexTile, mask=PE_MASK, <last>, ->DstTile<TSize>; B.IOR BaseGPR, zero, zero, ->zero; BSTOP","B.IOR BaseGPR, MinIndexGPR, MaxIndexGPR, ->zero (optional indexed range descriptor; RegSrc1=RegSrc2=zero preserves the legacy absent form)"],"exceptions":["Malformed bundle schema, nonzero unused B.IOR fields, unsupported datatype or layout, descriptor/shape mismatch, noncanonical predicate values, or an access fault rejects before effects."],"field_contracts":{"B.IOR.RegSrc0":{"ref":"PTO-FIELD-BLOCK-GPR-SELECTOR"},"B.IOR.RegSrc1":{"ref":"PTO-FIELD-BLOCK-GPR-SELECTOR"},"B.IOR.RegSrc2":{"ref":"PTO-FIELD-BLOCK-GPR-SELECTOR"}},"field_zero_meanings":{"B.IOR.RegSrc0":"The architectural zero register supplies GM base address zero.","B.IOR.RegSrc1":"The architectural zero GPR; with RegSrc2 it encodes an absent descriptor only in the no-GPR-mask first-record form.","B.IOR.RegSrc2":"The architectural zero GPR; with RegSrc1 it encodes an absent descriptor only in the no-GPR-mask first-record form."},"legality":["Non-packed transfer shapes match IndexTile; packed four-bit uses Data.ValidCol == 2 * Index.ValidCol and rejects incomplete pairs.","ROWMAJOR, CUBE_M16, and CUBE_M32 are accepted; CUBE_N8 is rejected.","Participating Local Tiles share the layout class and logical coordinates while retaining independent DataType, TSize, LB2, physical columns, and capacity.","B.IOR RegSrc0 supplies BaseGPR; RegSrc1, RegSrc2, and RegDst must encode zero.","A present range descriptor supplies signed 64-bit relative byte-displacement bounds, read from the current participating PE. The current request faults with Fault_TileLegality when MinIndex > MaxIndex, before its indexed memory or Tile destination effects; committed peer effects remain. Software certifies that every participating active indexed access start byte is within the inclusive bounds and that [Base+Min, Base+Max+AccessBytes) is nonwrapping in the 64-bit GM address domain; hardware does not validate each IndexTile value against the certificate."],"memory_effects":["Each indexed transaction loads one transfer element, or one packed byte containing the low then high logical nibble, at BaseGPR plus the byte displacement.","All valid addresses are preflighted before the first architectural effect."],"operands":[{"field":"DataType","role":"tile element data type selector"},{"field":"B.IOR.RegSrc0","role":"per-PE private-GPR GM base address"},{"field":"B.IOR.RegSrc1","role":"per-PE private-GPR zero selector"},{"field":"B.IOR.RegSrc2","role":"full-width signed range bound selector when the descriptor is present"}],"ordering":["Existing PTO memory ordering and implementation-defined duplicate-address serialization are unchanged.","The optional descriptor is a conservative indexed access-set summary only. Absence or incomparable/possibly aliased translated ranges retain conservative dependence handling; interval disjointness may remove only conflict edges permitted by the existing PTO memory model and never weakens independent ordering constraints."],"standalone_opcode":true,"state_effects":["The complete physical destination region is initialized to PadValue before active valid results are published.","On success the full physical destination region is defined; a failing attempt publishes no destination."]},"depends_on":["PTO-ARCH-MEMORY-MODEL-ORDERING","PTO-BLOCK-MODEL-DISPATCH-INDEXED-TLSU-RANGE-SCHEMA","PTO-BLOCK-MODEL-SCHEMA-BUNDLE-ENCODING"],"id":"PTO-BLOCK-BSTART-MGATHER","mnemonic":"BSTART.MGATHER","summary":"gather using explicit byte displacements.","surface":"block"}
